<h2 id="introduction">1. Introduction</h2>

<p>
Meridian Energy Management ("Meridian", "we", "us" or "our") is committed to protecting the privacy and personal information of our clients, prospective clients, suppliers, business partners, website visitors and other individuals who interact with us.
</p>

<p>
This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose and protect personal information when you visit our website, communicate with us, request our services, submit an enquiry or otherwise interact with Meridian.
</p>

<div class="highlight">
<p>
Meridian aims to handle personal information responsibly and in accordance with applicable South African privacy and data-protection requirements, including the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 ("POPIA"), where applicable.
</p>
</div>

<h2 id="information">2. Information We Collect</h2>

<p>
Depending on how you interact with Meridian, we may collect information that is reasonably necessary to provide our services, respond to enquiries, evaluate requirements and conduct legitimate business activities.
</p>

<h3>Information you provide directly</h3>

<ul>
<li>Name and surname</li>
<li>Company or organisation name</li>
<li>Job title or position</li>
<li>Email address</li>
<li>Telephone or WhatsApp number</li>
<li>Company registration information</li>
<li>Delivery or operational location</li>
<li>Product and fuel requirements</li>
<li>Requested volumes and specifications</li>
<li>Commercial or procurement requirements submitted through our website</li>
<li>Any other information voluntarily included in correspondence or enquiry forms</li>
</ul>

<h3>Technical information</h3>

<p>
When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically, such as browser type, device information, IP address, pages visited, approximate geographic information and website interaction data.
</p>

<p>
This information may be used to understand website performance, improve user experience, maintain security and analyse website traffic.
</p>

<h2 id="use">3. How We Use Personal Information</h2>

<p>
We may use personal information for legitimate business purposes, including:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Responding to enquiries and requests for quotations.</li>
<li>Understanding customer requirements.</li>
<li>Providing sourcing, procurement and energy supply services.</li>
<li>Communicating with clients, suppliers and business partners.</li>
<li>Preparing commercial proposals and quotations.</li>
<li>Coordinating logistics and supply requirements.</li>
<li>Managing business relationships.</li>
<li>Improving our website, services and customer experience.</li>
<li>Maintaining website and information security.</li>
<li>Complying with legal, regulatory and contractual obligations.</li>
<li>Preventing fraud, misuse or unlawful activity.</li>
</ul>

<p>
We will not use personal information for purposes that are incompatible with the purpose for which it was collected unless permitted or required by applicable law.
</p>

<h2 id="sharing">4. Information Sharing and Disclosure</h2>

<p>
Meridian does not sell personal information to third parties.
</p>

<p>
Where reasonably necessary for legitimate business purposes, information may be shared with trusted parties involved in providing services or conducting transactions. These may include:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Suppliers and product providers.</li>
<li>Logistics and transportation providers.</li>
<li>Storage, terminal or operational partners.</li>
<li>Professional advisers and service providers.</li>
<li>Technology and hosting providers.</li>
<li>Financial or payment service providers where applicable.</li>
<li>Government, regulatory or law-enforcement authorities where legally required.</li>
</ul>

<p>
Where information is shared with third parties, Meridian seeks to take reasonable steps to ensure that such information is handled appropriately and only for legitimate purposes.
</p>

<h2 id="security">5. Information Security</h2>

<p>
Meridian takes reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorised access, loss, misuse, alteration, disclosure or destruction.
</p>

<p>
However, no method of transmitting information over the internet or storing information electronically can be guaranteed to be completely secure. You should therefore exercise appropriate caution when submitting information online.
</p>

<h2 id="retention">6. Data Retention</h2>

<p>
We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, to maintain business records, fulfil contractual obligations, resolve disputes, comply with legal requirements or protect our legitimate interests.
</p>

<p>
The applicable retention period may differ depending on the nature of the information and the legal or business requirements associated with it.
</p>

<h2 id="rights">7. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

<p>
Subject to applicable law, individuals may have rights relating to their personal information, including the right to:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Request access to personal information held about them.</li>
<li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
<li>Request deletion where there is a lawful basis for doing so.</li>
<li>Object to certain processing activities.</li>
<li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
<li>Raise a concern regarding the handling of personal information.</li>
</ul>

<p>
Requests may be subject to applicable legal requirements, identity verification and reasonable administrative procedures.
</p>

<h2 id="cookies">8. Cookies and Website Technologies</h2>

<p>
Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to improve functionality, understand website usage and support analytics.
</p>

<p>
Cookies are small files stored on your device by a website. You may be able to control or disable cookies through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect some website functionality.
</p>

<h2 id="thirdparty">9. Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
Our website may use third-party services such as website hosting, analytics, security, communication or other technology providers.
</p>

<p>
These third parties may process certain technical or personal information as necessary to provide their services. Their processing may also be governed by their own privacy policies and terms.
</p>

<p>
Meridian seeks to use reputable service providers and to take reasonable steps to ensure that information is handled appropriately.
</p>

<h2 id="changes">10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

<p>
Meridian may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our services, technology, business practices or applicable legal requirements.
</p>

<p>
The latest version will be published on this page with an updated effective or revision date.
</p>

<h2 id="contact">11. Contact Us</h2>

<p>
If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to request access to personal information, or have a privacy-related concern, please contact Meridian using the details below.
</p>

